diagnosis_text:
The failure is in the control-plane on leaf_router_0_1: FRRouting (bgpd) is down, so 10.0.1.0/24 is not being advertised into the fabric. Mechanism: with no BGP from that leaf, both spines have no path to 10.0.1.0/24 and therefore cannot re-advertise it to the rest of the network. Each host’s default gateway (its local leaf) consequently lacks a route to the remote subnet and returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable,” which matches user symptoms. Localization: 
- On the endpoints, pings show “From 10.0.0.1” and “From 10.0.1.1” Net Unreachable, implicating both leaf gateways.
- On the spines, BGP to leaf_router_0_1 is not established (Active to 172.16.0.7/172.16.0.11) and their routes contain only 10.0.0.0/2
