[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_1
diagnosis_text:
The failure is in the control-plane on leaf_router_0_1: FRRouting (bgpd) is down, so 10.0.1.0/24 is not being advertised into the fabric. Mechanism: with no BGP from that leaf, both spines have no path to 10.0.1.0/24 and therefore cannot re-advertise it to the rest of the network. Each host’s default gateway (its local leaf) consequently lacks a route to the remote subnet and returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable,” which matches user symptoms. Localization: 
- On the endpoints, pings show “From 10.0.0.1” and “From 10.0.1.1” Net Unreachable, implicating both leaf gateways.
- On the spines, BGP to leaf_router_0_1 is not established (Active to 172.16.0.7/172.16.0.11) and their routes contain only 10.0.0.0/24.
- On leaf_router_0_1, the FRR service is inactive (dead), and vtysh reports “bgpd is not running.” Its routing table has only directly connected routes, no BGP-learned 10.0.0.0/24.

Root cause: FRR (bgpd) on leaf_router_0_1 is stopped, removing the advertisement of 10.0.1.0/24.

Corrective fix: Do not restart any spine. Restart FRR on leaf_router_0_1 (systemctl start frr; ensure it’s enabled). Verify BGP neighbors to both spines come up and that 10.0.1.0/24 is advertised. Afterward, leaf_router_0_0 should learn 10.0.1.0/24 via the spines, and host-to-host connectivity will be restored. If FRR does not load config, confirm /etc/frr/frr.conf contains router bgp 65201, neighbors to both spines, and network 10.0.1.0/24. 
=== END ===